│  **Madrid, Spain – Ultimate Travel Guide (February 14–16, 2026)**                                             │
│  **Traveler Interests: Art, History, Food, Culture**                                                          │
│                                                                                                               │
│  ---                                                                                                          │
│                                                                                                               │
│  ### **✈️ Flight Costs & Travel Tips**                                                                         │
│  - **Vienna to Madrid**: Round-trip flights average **€227–$362** (February 2026). Book 33+ days in advance   │
│  for best prices. Direct flights via **Japan Airlines (JL9442)** depart Feb 12, 2026, at 07:06. Consider      │
│  budget airlines like **Vueling** or **Iberia** for flexible options.                                         │
│  - **Accommodation**: Mid-range hotels in **Retiro Park** or **Salamanca** cost **€120–€180/night**. Budget   │
│  hostels in **Centro** start at **€40–€70/night**.                                                            │
│                                                                                                               │
│  ---                                                                                                          │
│                                                                                                               │
│  ### **🌤️ Weather Forecast (February 14–16, 2026)**                                                            │
│  - **Daytime**: 12–15°C (54–59°F), mild and comfortable.                                                      │
│  - **Nighttime**: 5–8°C (41–46°F).                                                                            │
│  - **Rain**: Occasional light rain; pack a compact umbrella and layer clothing.                               │
│                                                                                                               │
│  ---                                                                                                          │
│                                                                                                               │
│  ### **🖼️ Must-Visit Attractions & Cultural Hotspots**                                                         │
│  1. **Prado Museum** (World’s Top Art Collection):                                                            │
│     - **Highlight**: Velázquez’s *Las Meninas*, El Greco’s *View of Toledo*.                                  │
│     - **Pro Tip**: Book tickets online to skip lines.                                                         │
│                                                                                                               │
│  2. **Reina Sofía Museum**:                                                                                   │
│     - **Must-See**: Picasso’s *Guernica* (a must for art lovers).                                             │
│                                                                                                               │
│  3. **Royal Palace of Madrid**:                                                                               │
│     - **Tip**: Visit the **Spanish Riding School** for horseback performances (book tickets in advance).      │
│                                                                                                               │
│  4. **Barrio de Salamanca**:                                                                                  │
│     - **Local Secret**: Stroll through its 19th-century architecture and boutique shops.                      │
│                                                                                                               │
│  5. **Plaza Mayor**:                                                                                          │
│     - **Cultural Insight**: A vibrant square with historic buildings and daily street performers.             │
│                                                                                                               │
│  ---                                                                                                          │
│                                                                                                               │
│  ### **🕵️‍♀️ Hidden Gems & Off-the-Beaten-Path Spots**                                                           │
│  - **Cibeles Tower** (Torre de Cibeles): Panoramic views of the city from the 33rd floor.                     │
│  - **Museo del Romanticismo**: A quirky museum with 19th-century artifacts and a dollhouse.                   │
│  - **Moncloa Park**: A peaceful escape with cherry blossoms (in bloom early February).                        │
│  - **San Isidro District**: Quaint neighborhood with traditional tapas bars and artisan markets.              │
│                                                                                                               │
│  ---                                                                                                          │
│                                                                                                               │
│  ### **🍽️ Food & Drink: Local Flavors & Tips**                                                                 │
│  - **Tapas**:                                                                                                 │
│    - **La Latina**: Try *croquetas* (fried bread rolls) and *pimientos de Padrón*.                            │
│    - **Cervecería El Jaleo**: A historic spot for *tortilla española* and sangria.                            │
│  - **Churros & Chocolate**:                                                                                   │
│    - **Churrería Las Tercias** (Plaza Mayor) or **Churrería del Bajío** (near Plaza de España).               │
│  - **Wine Bars**:                                                                                             │
│    - **Cava 1890** (Barrio de las Letras): Affordable Rioja wine and small plates.                            │
│  - **Specialty**: Try *pulpo a la gallega* (Galician octopus) at **Restaurante Botín** (a 30-minute walk      │
│  from the city center).                                                                                       │
│                                                                                                               │
│  ---                                                                                                          │
│                                                                                                               │
│  ### **🎭 Special Events & Festivals (February 2026)**                                                        │
│  - **Madrid Fusión** (Mid-February): A food and design festival with pop-up restaurants and art               │
│  installations.                                                                                               │
│  - **Flamenco Shows**: Check **Teatro Lara** or **Casa de la Velada** for traditional performances.           │
│  - **Local Markets**: **Mercado de San Miguel** (daily) for fresh produce and street food.                    │
│                                                                                                               │
│  ---                                                                                                          │
│                                                                                                               │
│  ### **🛍️ Local Customs & Practical Tips**                                                                     │
│  - **Dining Etiquette**: Meals are leisurely; arrive 15–30 minutes late for tapas.                            │
│  - **Tipping**: 10% service charge is standard in restaurants; no need to round up.                           │
│  - **Transport**: Use **metro** (€1.50/ride) or **Madrid Travel Card** (€10/day for unlimited travel).        │
│  - **Safety**: Avoid carrying large bags; use secure metro compartments.                                      │
│                                                                                                               │
│  ---                                                                                                          │
│                                                                                                               │
│  ### **💰 Cost Overview**                                                                                     │
│  - **Accommodation**: €120–€180/night (mid-range), €40–€70/night (budget).                                    │
│  - **Eating Out**: €10–€20 for tapas, €15–€30 for a main course.                                              │
│  - **Activities**: €10–€15 for museum entry, free for many parks and plazas.                                  │
│                                                                                                               │
│  ---                                                                                                          │
│                                                                                                               │
│  ### **🌟 Final Recommendations**                                                                             │
│  - **Day 1 (Feb 14)**: Prado Museum → Retiro Park → Tapas in La Latina.                                       │
│  - **Day 2 (Feb 15)**: Royal Palace → Reina Sofía Museum → Dinner at Cava 1890.                               │
│  - **Day 3 (Feb 16)**: Cibeles Tower → San Isidro District → Shopping at Mercado de San Miguel.               │
